WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:02.549
- So there's a new question
at the red carpet this year.

00:00:02.549 --> 00:00:04.619
Forget who are you wearing?

00:00:04.619 --> 00:00:05.452
- Who are you wearing?

00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:06.337
- Who are you wearing this evening?

00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:08.107
- Who am I wearing, oh Givenchy.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.248
Do you do that to the guys?

00:00:10.248 --> 00:00:12.797
- Now it's why are you wearing?

00:00:12.797 --> 00:00:15.059
Because this year,
everybody's wearing black to

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:17.957
raise awareness of sexual
harassment in the industry.

00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:20.997
There are already a ton of
celebrities that have promised to

00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:22.827
wear black in support of the cause.

00:00:22.827 --> 00:00:24.648
- I'm definitely going to
be wearing black for the

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:26.608
Golden Globes and standing with the women.

00:00:26.608 --> 00:00:28.939
I'm bringing one of my
best friends with me and

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:30.986
she will be wearing black also.

00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:33.569
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:38.547
- So Golden Globes, why
are they all wearing black?

00:00:38.547 --> 00:00:42.441
- This year, after the
Harvey Weinstein story,

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:44.721
it kind of broke out in big public way.

00:00:44.721 --> 00:00:47.201
A lot of women in Hollywood
were looking for ways to

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:50.833
take action and move forward
and out of that came the

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:55.153
Time's Up Movement which was
founded by a bunch of very

00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:57.732
high-powered women in the
entertainment industry.

00:00:57.732 --> 00:01:01.313
Say Time's up, we're not
gonna do this anymore.

00:01:01.313 --> 00:01:02.182
We're not gonna let this happen.

00:01:02.182 --> 00:01:05.892
They have a legal fund and
one of the prongs of approach

00:01:05.892 --> 00:01:08.793
is to have people wear black
to the Golden Globes as

00:01:08.793 --> 00:01:10.772
a show of solidarity.

00:01:10.772 --> 00:01:14.292
- I think that there's a power
there that can be reached no

00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:18.513
other way except for when
people fly in formation,

00:01:18.513 --> 00:01:19.430
act as one.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:21.881
- We're taking this seriously.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.182
Here is a visual representation
of that on top of the

00:01:24.182 --> 00:01:27.441
other things that they're
trying to do to make change.

00:01:27.441 --> 00:01:29.782
- The whole sexual harassment subject

00:01:29.782 --> 00:01:31.513
should be completely condemned.

00:01:31.513 --> 00:01:35.892
There should be equal payment
and equal opportunities.

00:01:35.892 --> 00:01:38.113
- I can't remember any award
shows where everyone wore the

00:01:38.113 --> 00:01:41.833
same color dress but I'm
gonna be there in black.

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:45.319
- Fashion's always been a huge
part of award shows, right?

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:49.380
We have now a whole industry
of red carpet shows that happen

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.208
even before the award show happens.

00:01:51.208 --> 00:01:52.289
- Hours and hours.

00:01:52.289 --> 00:01:56.828
- Would you be my inaugural
Manicam, okay, right here.

00:01:56.828 --> 00:01:59.137
I love that natural look.

00:01:59.137 --> 00:02:00.885
- Congratulations, tell me
about your dress this evening.

00:02:00.885 --> 00:02:03.668
- Well, it's pink and
there are stars on it.

00:02:03.668 --> 00:02:05.566
- There are hours and
hours of shows that happen,

00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:08.348
sometimes are even longer than
the actual award show itself.

00:02:08.348 --> 00:02:11.136
Celebrities have really realized
that there's an opportunity

00:02:11.136 --> 00:02:14.228
on the red carpet to have a
more nuance conversation than

00:02:14.228 --> 00:02:16.840
the What are you wearing/who
are you wearing discussion.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.507
- Yeah, because they're hours long.

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.008
- Pretty much only for the women on

00:02:20.008 --> 00:02:21.736
red carpets at awards shows,

00:02:21.736 --> 00:02:23.655
there's so much emphasis
put on their fashion

00:02:23.655 --> 00:02:26.536
statements that they want to be like,

00:02:26.536 --> 00:02:28.917
"Yeah, you're gonna talk about
our fashion but like this

00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:31.448
time you have to mention how
it's connected to this big

00:02:31.448 --> 00:02:33.637
thing that's happening to everybody."

00:02:33.637 --> 00:02:35.517
- One of the things that has
happened in recent years is

00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:38.168
that celebrity women have
started a campaign to say

00:02:38.168 --> 00:02:41.116
ask her more which is to say, you know,

00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:43.397
ask me more than who am I
wearing on the red carpet.

00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:46.736
Women in the film industry want
to be taken more seriously.

00:02:46.736 --> 00:02:50.605
The want to be perceived as
more than just designer clothing

00:02:50.605 --> 00:02:52.285
hangers when their on the red carpet.

00:02:52.285 --> 00:02:54.009
- This is a movement to, ya know,

00:02:54.009 --> 00:02:55.880
say we're more than just our dresses.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.880
- Hashtag ask her more.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.800
- Highlight the fact that
women are multifaceted.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.800
That we can talk about the
world as much as we can

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.091
talk about our gowns.

00:03:04.091 --> 00:03:06.461
- Women wearing black this year
is kind of just an extension

00:03:06.461 --> 00:03:08.479
of what's been happening
in the past years.

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:11.541
- I think there's always been
people that have used fashion

00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:13.857
as a means to express political thought.

00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:18.017
Joy Villa who has wore a
dress at the Grammy's that was

00:03:18.017 --> 00:03:21.238
a maga-dress and had Trump on the train.

00:03:21.238 --> 00:03:24.399
Then, you know, we see people
like Salma Hayek wear things

00:03:24.399 --> 00:03:27.748
that are political or carry
signs because we are living in

00:03:27.748 --> 00:03:31.665
such a controversial
politically striated time.

00:03:32.685 --> 00:03:35.228
You're going to see a lot more
of that this year probably.

00:03:35.228 --> 00:03:37.148
- You're definitely gonna
watch the Golden Globes, right?

00:03:37.148 --> 00:03:38.927
- I'll be covering from the office.

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:40.947
- Are you gonna be wearing
black in solidarity?

00:03:40.947 --> 00:03:43.777
- Maybe, I hadn't thought about that.

00:03:43.777 --> 00:03:46.068
Maybe I'll, yeah, we'll see.

00:03:46.068 --> 00:03:48.651
(upbeat music)

00:03:52.668 --> 00:03:54.052
(sign creaking)

